## Status

The RPF9 table of contents (file names and tree) is encrypted (AES-CBC) and its
key is not yet public, so archive contents are read by carving rather than by the
directory. Texture stores (`TTPF`) are fully decoded. See
[docs/RPF9.md](docs/RPF9.md) for the format notes.
